id: karmic-boost
name: Karmic Boost
kind: karma
cost: 1
description: >
  You pour your heart and soul into the fight to ensure your desired outcome.
text: >
  After making a Combat Roll, when you know the result of the Clash it was
  involved in, you may roll an Extra Dice equal to your Greater Dice (before
  any modifications) and then increase the Dice Score by 1(bT). Apply this Dice
  Score to your Combat Roll. This may change the outcome of the Clash that
  Combat Roll was involved in.

---

# Taken after the Clash is settled, which is why the moment is
# clash-resolved and not combat-roll: the whole point is choosing once you
# know whether you need it.
# greaterDice is your Greater Dice before any modification, which is what
# the named amount reads.
# clash.combatRoll is what keeps this off a Skill Clash: the rule says "after
# making a Combat Roll", and Strike, Dodge and Wound are the Combat Rolls -
# a Thumb War is not one of them.
# clash.lost is what keeps it off a Wound Roll nobody answered. The rule wants
# "the Clash it was involved in", and an unopposed Wound Roll is not one - so
# there is no loser and this rules itself out. Power Flare answers the Wound
# with Might, and then there is a Clash and a loser, and this applies again.

[triggered/clash-resolved]
requires clash.lost && clash.combatRoll;
roll.dice += greaterDice;
roll.total += 1(bT);
